So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(x^{^{\Large\frac{1}{3}}}\right)=\dfrac13x^{^{\Large-\frac{2}{3}}}$, which can also be written as $\dfrac{1}{3(\sqrt[3]{x})^2}$.

Now let's plug $\blueD{x=8}$:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{1}{3(\sqrt[3]{\blueD8})^2}&=\dfrac{1}{3(2)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{3\cdot 4}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{12}
\end{align}$
